{
  "summary": "This experiment isolated the aggregation architecture by replacing avgpool with a transformer in the otherwise identical RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200 configuration (directly comparable to llm_summary_004). Validation accuracy of ~65.3% (F1 ~62.8%) is essentially unchanged from the avgpool result of ~65.0% (F1 ~62.8%), a negligible ~0.3-point difference suggesting that transformer aggregation does not substantially outperform simple average pooling and that ~65% may represent a practical ceiling for RNA-only multiprofile models under this encoder. It remains uncertain whether alternative encoders, the previously weak image modality in a multiprofile context, or cross-modal fusion could push beyond this level, and whether the near-equivalence of aggregation strategies would hold under different data scales or architectural combinations."
}

